Subject: [PATCH 07996/11362] [outer-loop] READ the gateway charge instead of
 modelling it (1.81%, not 3.69%) + restore 7 FABRICATION-GATE stamps a
 conductor overwrite stripped

STOP MODELLING THE CHARGE, READ IT. Every "gateway-charged" number this project
held was a MODEL that reconstructed the charge as offline_actions + resets
(optionally minus a free opening reset). Reading the arcade's OWN Card
(_read_gateway_card -> card.actions / card.resets / card.actions_by_level) over
48 cells: REAL median relative optimism 0.018097, mean 0.028887, min -0.018209
-- against the published model's 0.036903. The model is wrong on 17 of 44 cells
and SIGN-FLIPPED on 6, and it never understates (max signed error 0.058843).
A new G7 gate asserts agreement with the Card; it FAILS 17/44, and that failure
IS the correction (classified EXPECTED, n_failed_and_UNEXPECTED: 0).

WHY EVERY EARLIER CHECK MISSED IT: both "independent scorer paths" reconstructed
the charge from actions + resets - k, and NEITHER consulted the live Card. Their
44/44 agreement compared two implementations of the same unverified assumption.
Agreement between reconstructions is not evidence about the gateway.

THE MECHANISM IS POST-DEATH ACTIONS, NOT THE FREE OPENING RESET -- the wrong
intermediate answer this session published and then had to retract. A non-RESET
action taken while the game is already GAME_OVER or WIN returns frame=[]
(arcengine/base_game.py:204-216) and the scorecard update is gated on
len(resp.frame) > 0 (arc_agi/wrapper.py:187), so those actions are FREE at the
gateway while the model charged them. Measured: uncharged == empty_frame_actions
on 48/48 cells. The same gate is on the HTTP path (arc_agi/api.py:336), so this
is server behaviour, not an offline artifact. The free opening reset is real but
separate and much smaller.

Running tally on this one number, for the record: a 0-96% bound -> 4.62% -> 3.69%
-> 1.81%. Each layer shrank it; only the last stopped modelling.

A LIVE FABRICATION-GATE HOLE, RESTORED. The conductor re-runs experiments and
overwrites results/*.json IN PLACE. On this pass it silently dropped
flagged_adversarial: True from 7 artifacts (True -> None), 6 of which also lost
corrigendum_pending + corrigendum_note: exp1861, exp1938, exp2085, exp3734,
exp4162, exp4170, exp696. CLAUDE.md's fabrication gate requires capstone /
evidence-table / paper-v6 / headline-aggregation tasks to SKIP artifacts carrying
flagged_adversarial: true -- so stripping the stamp RE-ADMITS a quarantined
artifact to headline aggregation, silently, with no diff anyone reads. The stamps
were RE-VERIFIED against the CURRENT contents before restoring, not assumed:
adversarial_verify reports 1 flagged on all 7 NEW versions, so each determination
is live. Restored the stamp + corrigendum records; KEPT every re-run MEASUREMENT
number (fail-forward, never revert). Each file carries
flagged_adversarial_restoration_note + flagged_adversarial_restored_fields so the
restoration is auditable and cannot be mistaken for the original stamp.

STRUCTURAL FIX NOT DONE, FILED: the conductor should not overwrite artifacts in
place. Until it stops, this recurs on every re-run and the next occurrence will
again be invisible.

A THIRD STALE ON-DISK CLAIM CORRECTED (after the early-stop comment and the score
formula): arc_leaderboard_eval.py's comment asserted level_up_charged is "exactly
what the gateway's actions_by_level would hold". It now names the Card fields as
ground truth, records the 17/44 + 6-sign-flip refutation, keeps the model as a
labelled UPPER BOUND (it never understates), and warns against reintroducing the
framing. That comment edit drifted 4 artifacts -- the cost the rescore lane
declined to pay, paid here because a comment asserting refuted fidelity is worse
than a rebuild. All 4 rebuilt: 3 analyser passes plus the LIVE 48-cell capture,
0 non-clock diffs each, verdicts identical, REAL median 0.018097 reproduced
exactly (a determinism witness, not just a freshness stamp).

Also in this commit, from the review of the three 2026-07-26 lanes: "wins"
renamed to cells_with_at_least_one_levelup* (it fired on lv > 0, not on game
completion); cost level C stamped UNFALSIFIABLE_AS_CONSTRUCTED (single-element
ratio set); the throughput arm's UNDERPOWERED verdict attached inline where the
latency-vs-throughput decomposition is asserted; hardcoded n_seeds 1 -> derived 2
and p-floor 0.125 -> 0.0078; 4-dp rounding replaced with efficiency_*_precise
(tu93's 0.041667 was literally 0.0003/0.0072); a tests_and_mutation_proofs block
(10 mutations, 10 caught, 0 escaped) replacing prose assertions; top-level
measurement_wall_s 9649.5; GATEWAY_ACCURATE renamed MODELLED across 32 keys; and
the competition_mode residual labelled so every figure is declared a LOWER BOUND
there. Plus a freshness-lint crash on list-shaped rows_sources -- the same
field-shape class as the QA-Layer origin incident.

NOT FIXED, disclosed: an xdist worker crash makes a full-suite failure set
unobtainable (both isolated reproductions were negative; needs full-suite load).
No deselect added -- CLAUDE.md forbids skipping tests, and a permanent skip trades
a visible crash for an invisible gap.

Verify: 87 passed across the 6 affected suites; adversarial_verify 0 flagged;
arc_orphan_solver_lint OK (65 modules in the live closure); artifact_freshness_lint
